CS1,0 $   Key to Hebeloma section Hebeloma (alpine or arctic)

1,5 $ Spores amygdaloid with dextrinoidity D2 or D3
1,2 $ Spores with dextrinoidity D0 or D1, amygdaloid or not

2,0 $ Number of full length lamellae (L) < 30 and pileus with a matting of short soft hairs $ H. pubescens
2,3 $ Number of full length lamellae > 30 or if < 30 then pileus with at most a few hairs at margin

3,0 $ Ave. spore length < 10 µm or ave. spore width < 6 µm and spores ellipsoid, only rarely amygdaloid $ H. mesophaeum
3,4 $ Ave. spore length > 10 µm and ave. spore width > 6 µm or if spores smaller then most spores ellipsoid but many amygdaloid, always with Salicaceae

4,0 $ Spores with some clear ornamentation (O1, O2) and an indistinct but clear reaction in Melzer’s Reagent (Dl) $ H. dunense
4,0 $ Spores showing almost no ornamentation, even under immersion (O1) or completely indextrinoid (D0) $ H. marginatulum

5,0 $ Number of full length lamellae (L) < 40 $ H. oreophilum
5,6 $ Number of full length lamellae (L) < 40

6,0 $ Ave. spore length > 15µm $ H. grandisporum
6,7 $ Ave. spore length < 15 µm

7,0 $ Spore papilla distinctly present and many spores limoniform $ H. fuscatum
7,8 $ Spore papilla at most weakly present and spores rarely limoniform

8,0 $ Ave. spore width < 7.5 µm $ H. nigellum
8,0 $ Ave. spore width > 7.5 µm $ H. spetsbergense



CS2,0 $     Key to Hebeloma subsection Crustuliniformia (alpine or arctic)

1,8 $ Number of full length lamellae >= 60 and average spore length <11 µm
1,2 $ Number of full length lamellae < 60 or average spore length >11 µm

2,0 $ Number of full length lamellae < 40, spore length >=11 µm and spores with distinct papilla $ H. alpinum
2,3 $ Any of the above conditions not satisfied [Number of full length lamellae < 40, spore length >11 µm and spores with distinct papilla]

3,0 $ Spores O3 and D2 and not D1 $ H. salicicola
3,4 $ Spores not O3 or not D2 or D1

4,0 $ Average width of cheilocystidia apex < 8.5 µm $ H. aurantioumbrinum
4,5 $ Average width of cheilocystidia apex >= 8.5 µm

5,6 $ Average cheilocystidium ratio A/B > 1.8
5,7 $ Average cheilocystidium ratio A/B < 1.8

6,0 $ Spores Ol or O2, few if any spores O3 $ H. louiseae
6,0 $ A large number of spores O3 $ H. minus

7,0 $ Majority of spores Ol and average spore length <= 12 µm $ H. perexiguum
7,0 $ At least some spores O2 and average spore length >12 µm $ H. pallidolabiatum

8,0 $ Average width of cheilocystidia apex > 9 µm $ H. geminatum
8,0 $ Average width of cheilocystidia apex > 8 µm and <= 9 µm $ H. aanenii/H. geminatum
8,0 $ Average width of cheilocystidia apex < 8 µm $ H. aanenii

